 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Open the pantry before you leave, and keep it cracked. Bears are drawn by smell, and open food lets them know it a good place. Keep it as far away as you can, on a higher spot if there are trees, or against a steep slope if there aren't. That makes it harder for them to reach. Don't get in the tent, bears often back off if you stand your ground. Stay calm, back away slowly, and tell park staff as soon as possible. Most people never have problem. The main thing is to keep your food locked away.",
